{
  "id": 297,
  "name": "transgender children and young people having access to gender affirming healthcare",
  "description": "the federal government should not restrict access to gender affirming healthcare for transgender people under the age of eighteen, rather they should leave healthcare matters in the hands of the professional bodies responsible for administering such healthcare (e.g., the Australian Medical Association, the Australian Psychological Society, etc.)",
